   $q$Which is the factored form of $27x^3 + 64$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(3x + 4)(9x^2 - 24x + 16)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"doubled-middle-term"},{"text":"$(3x - 4)(9x^2 + 12x + 16)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-difference-of-cubes"},{"text":"$(3x + 4)(9x^2 - 12x + 16)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$(3x + 4)(9x^2 + 12x + 16)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-middle-sign"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(3x + 4)(9x^2 - 12x + 16)$$q$, $q$With $a = 3x$ and $b = 4$, $a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2) = (3x + 4)(9x^2 - 12x + 16)$. Writing $-24x$ doubles the middle term as if squaring a binomial, but the cube pattern uses $ab$, not $2ab$.$q$, 'draft', null)
