   $q$By writing $x^4 + 4 = (x^2 + 2)^2 - 4x^2$, which is a factorization of $x^4 + 4$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(x^2 + 2x + 2)(x^2 - 2x + 2)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$(x^2 + 2x + 2)(x^2 + 2x - 2)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error"},{"text":"$(x^2 + 2)^2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-middle-term"},{"text":"$(x + 2)(x - 2)(x^2 + 1)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-sum-as-difference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(x^2 + 2x + 2)(x^2 - 2x + 2)$$q$, $q$The rewritten form is a difference of squares with $a = x^2 + 2$ and $b = 2x$, so it equals $(x^2 + 2 + 2x)(x^2 + 2 - 2x)$. The choice $(x^2 + 2)^2$ expands to $x^4 + 4x^2 + 4$, so it ignores the $-4x^2$ that was subtracted.$q$, 'draft', null)
